  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "A coin was tossed multiple times.\nThe ratio of times when the coin landed heads up to the total number of tosses is $4:9.$\nIf the coin landed heads up $16$ times, how many times did it land tails up?",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $4:9$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{9}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of heads, and the denominator represents the total number of tosses.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $16$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 4}{9\\times 4}=\\frac{16}{36}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coin was tossed $36$ times in total. \nSo, the number of tails is\n\n$$\n36-16=20.\n$$",
